    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d369-a2">

                <pb facs="0741" n="631" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg631"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 255.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoff to Mr.
                            Ryan.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-02-15"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 15,
                        1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I received yours of 8th, and at the same
                    time a telegram from J. H. Stilphen saying his case had been removed to Vera
                    Cruz for reexamination, to the district court, and I accordingly went to the
                    court and saw the clerk, and he said it was there and under examination, but
                    when it would be decided it was out of his power to tell.</p>
                <p>The captain seems very impatient, as he has his $200 bail up and he wants it back
                    in his pocket again. He says the court at Minatitlan say they find nothing
                    against him. Captain has sailed from Minatitlan for New Orleans at present.</p>
                <p>Yours truly,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph D. Hoff.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
